# The start command, and buildpacks need it stated.
#
# Without this the image BUILDS AND RUNS AND DOES NOTHING: Paketo's python-start
# buildpack looks for a conventional entrypoint — main.py, app.py, manage.py — or
# a Procfile, finds neither, and produces an image whose web process is empty.
# The container then exits 0 immediately, so the pod CrashLoopBackOffs with no
# logs and the probe reports "connection refused". Nothing anywhere says "no
# start command".
#
# `run.py` is the entrypoint by convention in this template (see its docstring);
# this is the line that tells the platform so.
web: python run.py
